I go inside the museum.
It is very quiet here.
I go near the ticket window.
There is no crowd there right now.
A clerk is sitting there.
"Hello sir, give me one ticket please," I say.
"Yes madam."
"Are you a foreigner?" he asks.
"Yes, I am from Mexico."
"How many rupees is the ticket?" I ask.
"Five hundred rupees," he says.
I give him five hundred rupees.
He gives me the ticket.
I look at this ticket.
"Sir, are the upstairs galleries open right now?" I ask.
"Yes, those galleries are open," he says.
"First you go to this main hall."
He points a finger straight ahead.
"Thank you," I say and go forward.
Five months ago, I used to feel afraid of such new places.
But now I feel good.
The silence of this building spreads around me.
